            0.437,
            0.097,
            0.698,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make your own ORS!"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.126,
            0.868,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ORS—Oral Rehydration Solution—",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is used to treat dehydration due to diarrhoea or other illnesses. These ready-made ORS packets are available in primary health centres and also in the market. Each packet is dissolved in a litre of water before use. If these are not available, ORS can be prepared at home by mixing six teaspoons of sugar and half a teaspoon of common salt in one litre of boiled and cooled water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.283,
            0.423,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do liquids like oil, vinegar and honey dissolve in water? Ex"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plore",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.633,
            0.292,
            0.831,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What about the gases present in water?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.532,
            0.886,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some liquids get completely mixed with water. Some do not mix with water and form a separate layer when left undisturbed for some time. Similarly, some gases are soluble in water whereas others are not. For example, oxygen gas dissolves in water. It is very important for the survival of animals and plants that live in water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.667,
            0.556,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.3.5 How heavy or light?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.707,
            0.56,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 6.8: Let us measure"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.739,
            0.883,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take three identical paper cups (or bowls). Fill each cup half with the provided materials."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.785,
            0.884,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fill one with water and mark it as ‘A’, second with sand and mark it as ‘B’, and the third with pebbles and mark it as ‘C’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.853,
            0.883,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Predict which one would be heavier and which one would be lighter?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 13,
